del used in ULMFit, which uses dropout tuning strategies.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Natural language inference': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The task of determining the relationship between two sentences.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'BookCorpus': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used to train BERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'English Wikipedia': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used to train BERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Next Sentence Prediction': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['A language modeling task that BERT is trained on, where the model predicts whether a sentence follows the preceding sentence in the text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Gradual Unfreezing': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A technique used during fine-tuning to prevent catastrophic forgetting, as proposed by Howard and Ruder (2018).'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Fine-tuning BERT': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The process of adapting a pre-trained BERT model to a specific downstream task, such as text classification, by further training it on a task-specific dataset.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Regression tasks': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['A type of machine learning task where the goal is to predict a continuous numerical value, as opposed to classification tasks which predict a category.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'BERT-base': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A version of the BERT model with 12 encoder layers, a hidden size of 768, 12 multi-head attention heads, and a total of 110M parameters.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'BERT-large': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A version of the BERT model with 24 encoder layers, a hidden size of 1024, 16 multi-head attention heads, and a total of 340M parameters.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Experiments with BERT configurations': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The series of experiments conducted to evaluate different configurations of